{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966197-questions-regarding-the-venombite-kith-the-toxicity-rules-and-grappling","id":966197,"title":"Questions regarding the Venombite kith, the Toxicity rules and grappling!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T07:16:28-07:00","id":966197,"title":"Questions regarding the Venombite kith, the Toxicity rules and grappling!","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> For the upcoming weekend I am intending to play a little bit of Changeling with the latest edition and I am considering making a Venombite, because they seem like a lot of fun!<br /> <br /> Here's a quote from the released Kith's list regarding the venombite. It's about delivering the venom.<br /> <br /> <i>Spend a point of Glamour to deliver a venomous bite when using a damage move as part of a grapple (see p. XX). If successful, the Venombite causes lethal damage and injects the victim with venom with a Toxicity rating equal to her Wyrd.</i><br /> <br /> So to the questions...<br /> <br /> 1: When grappling, there are several different effects you can put on your foe. One of them is restrain. If you restrain someone in a grapple in round two of the fight(without using gear to help you), must you continue &quot;only&quot; holding them in round three or could you apply your venom while maintaining the restrain from the previous round?<br /> 2: It says the Venombite causes lethal damage. Is this for the &quot;damage&quot; roll AND the toxin, or simply the toxin? Like, say if I roll five successes on my grapple for damage, do I deal five lethal damage and then apply a toxin that also deals lethal?<br /> 3: Is it possible for a Venombite to deliver a non-lethal venom, like a knock-out venom (aka Bashing damage)?<br /> 4: The rules for Toxicity on page 182 in the World of Darkness Core rule-book are a little bit confusing to me (could be because English is not my native language) but the read goes as this.<br /> <br /> (My bold)<br /> <i>Once delivered, the poison automatically deals damage (usually lethal, but a knockout gas could cause bashing) equal to its toxicity level. Some substances inflict damage only once. Others might inflict it for a number of turns or once per hour until purged or until the effect runs its course.<b> It could be possible</b> to resist the effects of such substances by rolling Stamina + Resolve in a reflexive and contested action. If more successes are rolled than damage is inflicted by the toxin, damage is ignored completely. If damage is equal to higher than success rolled, all damage is delivered as normal. Such a contested roll might occur once or in each period in which a toxin causes harm.</i><br /> <br /> Now, I can read this as either the resistance rules against poisons go for everything, or it only goes for damage-over-time poisons. Am I understanding the rules correct in that once a Venombite's poison is delivered, there's nothing you can do but take the damage, or do you roll Stamina+Resolve as if it was a damage-over-time poison?<br /> <br /> Thank you for all the help you can give me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T07:38:20-07:00","id":966750,"title":"","content":"And two bonus questions!<br /> <br /> Do I understand the template rules correctly if I interpret it that grappling changelings is more or less pointless, as all they have to do is pop a Glamor and then the hold breaks?<br /> <br /> Or well, it says a Clash of Wills-test is to be resolved, but how does a Changeling Clash of Wills-test come off? What abilities are used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T12:37:09-07:00","id":966863,"title":"","content":"1: You cannot maintain a restraining hold and also deal damage without special merits unless you roll an exceptional success. However, given that you don't need your hands free to bite, I would check with your ST if they would permit it. <br /> <br /> 2: I believe you deal damage from the bite and inflict toxin in addition.<br /> <br /> 3: The toxin is always lethal. If you want the option to deal bashing you can ask your ST how they'd handle that.<br /> <br /> 4: I would use the Updated Toxicity rules from the Chronicles of Darkness book, since the Changeling playtest is meant to work with second edition mechanics.<br /> <br /> Here's the relevant bit: <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT\">To resist the damage, make a reflexive Stamina + Resolve \u2013 Toxicity roll. Each success reduces the damage taken by one. </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Bonus: I would recommend getting the Potent Kith merit, since most of Venombite's blessings scale with Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T12:52:42-07:00","id":966871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966197-questions-regarding-the-venombite-kith-the-toxicity-rules-and-grappling?p=966863#post966863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus: I would recommend getting the Potent Kith merit, since most of Venombite's blessings scale with Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering that already!<br /> Any knowledge on whether there's any point to trying to grapple any changelings, seeing how they can spend a glamor to get free? Would it be better to simply ditch that if you intended to make a character that was decent at fighting other changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:16:17-07:00","id":966883,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say it's pointless, since Clash of Wills means you should theoretically have even odds of beating someone with the same Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Usually Clash of Wills is Attribute or Skill + Powerstat, but it doesn't specify a pool here. You could just roll Wyrd vs Wyrd, or have both characters add their Wyrd to the grapple test. You could also take inspiration from the Sealing rules and allow another Changeling to spend a glamour to cancel out the attempt or it automatically succeeds.<br /> <br /> Basically, there's not a hard rule in the mechanics as currently written. Talk to your ST and figure out something that seems fair. If you build a Changeling to grapple, they should be able to grapple other Changelings successfully most of the time unless the other Changeling is much more powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:19:08-07:00","id":966886,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your answers!<br /> <br /> I guess we'll just have to wait until the official rules are out to find out just how Clash of Wills will work for Lings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T20:33:44-07:00","id":967120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966197-questions-regarding-the-venombite-kith-the-toxicity-rules-and-grappling?p=966750#post966750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or well, it says a Clash of Wills-test is to be resolved, but how does a Changeling Clash of Wills-test come off? What abilities are used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that mechanics sidebars aren't typically repeated in the same book, I'm going to put money on the one in the Contracts spoiler.<br /> <br /> It's a little ambiguously phrased, but I'm inclined to suspect that the general reading for things that aren't Finesse-Attribute-based Contracts is Wyrd + an appropriate Finesse Attribute \u2014 Dexterity being the go-to for getting out of a physical grapple.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T00:27:22-07:00","id":967215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/966197-questions-regarding-the-venombite-kith-the-toxicity-rules-and-grappling?p=967120#post967120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that mechanics sidebars aren't typically repeated in the same book, I'm going to put money on the one in the Contracts spoiler.<br /> <br /> It's a little ambiguously phrased, but I'm inclined to suspect that the general reading for things that aren't Finesse-Attribute-based Contracts is Wyrd + an appropriate Finesse Attribute \u2014 Dexterity being the go-to for getting out of a physical grapple.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh! I didn't realize there was one in the contracts-spoilers part. I'll go read it right away.<br /> <br /> Thank you Satchel :3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}